      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover_Plains%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The New York and Harlem Railroad reached Dover Plains in 1852, making the town the line’s northern terminus until the track was extended farther north to Chatham.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        8
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover_Plains%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Old Drover’s Inn, opened in 1750 as a tavern, still welcomes guests today as a bed‑and‑breakfast with a restaurant.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://destinationdutchess.com/town/dover",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Dover Plains Library, founded around 1899, was added to the National Register of Historic Places in 2010.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        9,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover_Plains%2C_New_York",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "Metro‑North’s Harlem Line station in Dover Plains brings commuters straight into New York City every weekday.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dover_Plains%2C_New_York",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The Dover Plains Library began as a small collection in 1899 and has grown into a community hub that preserves the town’s history.",
